          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EMoving to Umbraco from another CMS is a big step. Done well, it gives you a cleaner site and happier editors. Done badly, it can cost you search rankings and months of rework. This session helps you get it right the first time.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWe cover content mapping, from old page types to new document types. We explain how to plan URL redirects so visitors and search engines find their way. We look at what to automate, what to move by hand and what to leave behind. We also discuss how to keep editors involved throughout the project.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EIncludes lessons learned from real migrations, good and bad. You will hear what we would do again and what we would avoid. There is time at the end for questions about your own migration plans.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "settingsData": [],
